WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:10.347
[MUSIC]

2
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:19.236
The short straddle seller is hoping for
a lack of movement in the price of

3
00:00:19.236 --> 00:00:23.020
the underlying shares and
is indifferent to direction.

4
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.500
It is a fairly pure ban on decreasing
volatility, and benefits from decay.

5
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:35.048
A short straddle is created when
an investor sells an equal number of calls

6
00:00:35.048 --> 00:00:37.810
and ports with the same strike and
expiration.

7
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:44.042
It may be used when investors expect
a decrease in either implied volatility or

8
00:00:44.042 --> 00:00:47.620
a lack of movement in the price
of the underlying equity.

9
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:53.662
Profit is limited to the initial premium
received while loss is potentially

10
00:00:53.662 --> 00:00:54.470
unlimited.

11
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.303
The direction of the stock does
not matter to the straddle seller,

12
00:00:59.303 --> 00:01:00.790
as long as the movement up or

13
00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:04.690
down from the strike stays within
the price received for the straddle.

14
00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.475
The maximum gain is
the cost of the trade and

15
00:01:08.475 --> 00:01:11.260
occurs if the stock closes
at the strike price.

16
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:14.801
Time decay helps a straddle seller.

17
00:01:14.801 --> 00:01:19.528
The combination has two breakeven
points equal to the strike price plus

18
00:01:19.528 --> 00:01:24.270
the cost of the trade, and the strike
price minus the cost of the trade.

19
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:30.264
The straddle seller, loses money if the
underlying price exceeds a range around

20
00:01:30.264 --> 00:01:33.555
the strike price,
beyond the total premium received.

21
00:01:33.555 --> 00:01:39.985
[MUSIC]